# Field table: Japannext PTS ITCH Market Data Specification (Equities), version 2.02,
# last updated July 2, 2026 (JNX ITCH 2.02). Offsets are 0-based within the message,
# as the specification tables them.
#
# No length prefix: the ITCH tables have none. ITCH is carried either in a MoldUDP64
# Message Block, whose 2-byte length belongs to MoldUDP64 (moldudp64.tbl), or as the
# payload of a SoupBinTCP Sequenced Data Packet (glimpse.tbl, soup::from_jnx). The
# reader frames the message; decode() is called on its first byte.
#
# The specification does not state message totals. Each @size is the last row's
# offset plus its length, from the table.
@venue jnx
@endian big
@pad space
# JNX ITCH 2.02, section 3: Integer is unsigned big-endian; Alpha is left-justified,
# right-padded with spaces. Price and Quantity fields are typed Integer in the tables.
@type Integer uint
@type Alpha char

### itch::from_jnx

MessageType T 0 1 # TimestampSecondsMessage: seconds part of the timestamp, sent for every second in which another message is sent (JNX ITCH 2.02, 4.1, p. 3-4)
@size 5
TimestampSeconds Integer 1 4 # Seconds past midnight of the day the trading session started

MessageType S 0 1 # SystemEventMessage: data feed, system and market events (4.2, p. 4)
@size 10
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
Group Alpha 5 4 # Order book group: DAY J-Market daytime, NGHT J-Market nighttime, DAYX X-Market, DAYU U-Market; blank if system-wide
SystemEvent Alpha 9 1 # O start of messages, S start of system hours, Q start of market hours, M end of market hours, E end of system hours, C end of messages (Table 1)

MessageType L 0 1 # PriceTickSizeMessage: one row of a price tick size table; sent before Orderbook Directory Messages (4.3, p. 4-5)
@size 17
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
PriceTickSizeTableId Integer 5 4 # Price tick size table identifier
PriceTickSize Integer 9 4 # Price tick size
PriceStart Integer 13 4 # Start of the price range for this tick size

MessageType R 0 1 # OrderbookDirectoryMessage: an order book available for trading; sent at the start of each trading day (4.4, p. 5)
@size 45
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderbookId Alpha 5 4 # Securities Identification Code Committee (SICC) code
OrderbookCode Alpha 9 12 # ISIN
Group Alpha 21 4 # Order book group: DAY, NGHT, DAYX, DAYU
RoundLotSize Integer 25 4 # Shares in a round lot
PriceTickSizeTableId Integer 29 4 # Price tick size table identifier
PriceDecimals Integer 33 4 # Decimal places in price fields; value is 1
UpperPriceLimit Integer 37 4 # Maximum tradable price
LowerPriceLimit Integer 41 4 # Minimum tradable price

MessageType H 0 1 # TradingStateMessage: trading state of an order book; spin before start of system hours, then changes (4.5, p. 6)
@size 14
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderbookId Alpha 5 4 # SICC code
Group Alpha 9 4 # Order book group: DAY, NGHT, DAYX, DAYU
TradingState Alpha 13 1 # T trading, V suspended

MessageType Y 0 1 # ShortSellingPriceRestrictionStateMessage: short selling price restriction state of an order book (4.6, p. 6-7)
@size 14
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderbookId Alpha 5 4 # SICC code
Group Alpha 9 4 # Order book group: DAY, NGHT, DAYX, DAYU
ShortSellingState Alpha 13 1 # 0 no price restriction, 1 price restriction in effect

MessageType A 0 1 # OrderAddedMessage: Order Added Message - No Attributes; an order added to the displayable book, or a reference price when Order Number is 0 (4.7.1, p. 7)
@size 30
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderNumber Integer 5 8 # Order number, unique per day per order book group; 0 is a reference price message
BuySellIndicator Alpha 13 1 # B buy, S sell; ignore if reference price message
Quantity Integer 14 4 # Shares added to the book; ignore if reference price message
OrderbookId Alpha 18 4 # SICC code
Group Alpha 22 4 # Order book group: DAY, NGHT, DAYX, DAYU
Price Integer 26 4 # Order price, 1 decimal place; reference price message: 0x7FFFFFFF means none available

MessageType F 0 1 # OrderAddedWithAttributesMessage: an order with market-specific attributes added to the displayable book (4.7.2, p. 8)
@size 35
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderNumber Integer 5 8 # Order number, unique per day per order book group
BuySellIndicator Alpha 13 1 # B buy, S sell
Quantity Integer 14 4 # Shares added to the book
OrderbookId Alpha 18 4 # SICC code
Group Alpha 22 4 # Order book group: DAY, NGHT, DAYX, DAYU
Price Integer 26 4 # Order price, 1 decimal place
Attribution Alpha 30 4 # Reserved, always blank
OrderType Alpha 34 1 # Q DLP order

MessageType E 0 1 # OrderExecutedMessage: a resting order fully or partly executed; price is the resting order's (4.8, p. 8)
@size 25
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderNumber Integer 5 8 # Order executed
ExecutedQuantity Integer 13 4 # Shares executed
MatchNumber Integer 17 8 # Match number, unique per day per order book group

MessageType D 0 1 # OrderDeletedMessage: an order cancelled; remove it from the book (4.9, p. 9)
@size 13
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderNumber Integer 5 8 # Order cancelled

MessageType U 0 1 # OrderReplacedMessage: an order replaced by one with a new order number (4.10, p. 9)
@size 29
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OriginalOrderNumber Integer 5 8 # Order replaced
NewOrderNumber Integer 13 8 # Order number of the replacement
Quantity Integer 21 4 # New displayed quantity
Price Integer 25 4 # New price

### end
